 response in human MCF7 breast cancer cells</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><year>2002</year><volume>293</volume><fpage>622</fpage><lpage>628</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12054648</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0006-291X(02)00205-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waxler</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obesity and cancer susceptibility in mice</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>1960</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>760</fpage><lpage>766</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kodell</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Medina</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Accelerated appearance of chemically induced mammary carcinomas in obese yellow (Avy/A) (BALB/c X VY) F1 hybrid mice</article-title><source>J Toxicol Environ Health</source><year>1982</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>142</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6290678</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klurfeld</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lloyd</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Welch</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tulp</surname><given-names>OL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kritchevsky</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reduction of enhanced mammary carcinogenesis in LA/N-cp (corpulent) rats by energy restriction</article-title><source>Proc So